{"statements": [
  {
    "id": "3.4.13a",
    "type": "RULE",
    "force": "LEGAL",
    "force_from": "text (\"required to\")",
    "text": "a driver MUST reduce the speed of the vehicle AND proceed with [?caution] WHEN the driver is approaching an emergency vehicle that is stopped with its red or red and blue lights flashing OR a tow truck with its amber lights flashing in the same direction of the driver's travel",
    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "m78",
        "quote": "When approaching any emergency vehicle that is stopped with its red, or red and blue, lights flashing or a tow truck with its amber lights flashing in the same direction of your travel, you are required to reduce the speed of your vehicle and proceed with caution."
      }
    ],
    "flags": [
      {
        "code": "J",
        "span": "caution",
        "note": "No stated measure of the level of caution required."
      }
    ],
    "links": [],
    "note": null
  },
  {
    "id": "3.4.13b",
    "type": "RULE",
    "force": "LEGAL",
    "force_from": "text (\"required to\")",
    "text": "a driver MUST move into a lane away from the emergency vehicle or tow truck WHEN the driver is approaching an emergency vehicle that is stopped with its red or red and blue lights flashing OR a tow truck with its amber lights flashing in the same direction of the driver's travel AND the roadway has two or more lanes of traffic in the same direction of the driver's travel ONLY IF it is [?safe] to do so",
    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "m79",
        "quote": "When the roadway has two or more lanes of traffic in the same direction of your travel, you are required to move into a lane away from the emergency vehicle or tow truck, if safe to do so, in addition to reducing the speed of your vehicle and proceeding with caution."
      },
      {
        "id": "m78",
        "quote": "When approaching any emergency vehicle that is stopped with its red, or red and blue, lights flashing or a tow truck with its amber lights flashing in the same direction of your travel, you are required to reduce the speed of your vehicle and proceed with caution."
      }
    ],
    "flags": [
      {
        "code": "J",
        "span": "safe",
        "note": "No observable test for when it is safe to change lanes."
      }
    ],
    "links": [
      "3.4.13a"
    ],
    "note": "The \"in addition to reducing the speed of your vehicle and proceeding with caution\" clause refers back to 3.4.13a; the lane change is an extra duty on top of the speed reduction. The condition about the stopped emergency vehicle or tow truck comes from the section heading and m78, which m79 references without restating the full description."
  }
]}
